from pathlib import Path
import json, datetime, html

DATE='2026-08-03'; STAMP='20260803'
OUT=Path('/root/Projects/artifact-library/artifacts/daily-ingest'); OUT.mkdir(parents=True,exist_ok=True)
lanes=[
{'slug':'model-portfolio-change-control','title':'Model Portfolio Change Control','rationale':'A coverage gap between model-choice governance and day-to-day operations: two fresh GitHub changes make model retirement and role-scoped access concrete administrative work rather than a quarterly policy exercise.','readout':'Model selection is now a moving operational dependency. GitHub simultaneously deprecated two Copilot models and opened team-targeted model policy preview; keep a tested fallback map and treat access rules as deployment configuration.','items':[
('Gemini 2.5 Pro and Gemini 3 Flash deprecated','https://github.blog/changelog/2026-07-31-gemini-2-5-pro-and-gemini-3-flash-deprecated','release','2026-07-31','GitHub removed Gemini 2.5 Pro and Gemini 3 Flash from all Copilot experiences, directing users to Gemini 3.1 Pro Preview and Gemini 3.6 Flash.','A model picker is not a stable interface. Prompts, latency assumptions, and output review expectations need an owned replacement path.','Buildn: add model IDs and fallback acceptance tests to every agent runbook. Client work: prepare a one-page migration note before a preferred model disappears.','Suggested replacements can differ in behavior and preview status; validate task quality, cost, and access before changing defaults.','Inventory Copilot workflows that name either deprecated model; run a representative task on the replacement.'),
('Enterprise teams model policy targeting','https://github.blog/changelog/2026-07-31-enterprise-teams-model-policy-targeting-in-public-preview','release','2026-07-31','GitHub’s public preview moves optional-model access from organizations to enterprise teams, with a baseline Enabled / Disabled / Optional policy.','It enables role-based frontier-model pilots without granting every employee the same catalog.','Buildn: propose a “pilot / production / prohibited” model matrix. Client work: scope privileged models to trained delivery teams.','Access is additive: membership in any enabled team grants the model everywhere; organization-level settings deactivate in preview mode.','Model a test team and its memberships before enabling the preview.'),
('Managing availability of Copilot models','https://docs.github.com/enterprise-cloud@latest/copilot/how-tos/administer-copilot/manage-for-enterprise/manage-availability-of-default-models','docs','unknown','GitHub documents the enterprise baseline and the migration implications of team mode.','The documentation provides the control-plane checklist needed to turn the preview into an auditable rollout.','Buildn: capture the pre-switch policy export. Client work: assign model ownership to enterprise administrators.','Rollback restores the prior state, not policy edits made after entering team mode.','Record baseline settings and an owner before any preview opt-in.') ]},
{'slug':'private-agent-channel-controls','title':'Private Agent Channel Controls','rationale':'A neglected collaboration lane with practical fresh signal: targeted in-channel responses have reached Teams, while device-scoped Copilot remote-control policies provide a complementary boundary for where an operator can take over.','readout':'Agents need a private path for permissions and progress, plus a deliberate boundary for remote control. Use targeted messages for sensitive prompts and restrict takeover-capable sessions to managed devices.','items':[
('Chat SDK reactions and ephemeral messages on Teams','https://vercel.com/changelog/chat-sdk-reactions-and-ephemeral-messages-on-teams','release','unknown','Vercel Chat SDK’s Teams adapter now supports reactions, targeted ephemeral messages, author emails, custom token factories, and better conversation routing.','Permission requests and private diagnostics no longer need to spill into a shared project channel; reactions can make long-running work legible.','Buildn: acknowledge intake with a reaction, send approval prompts privately, and publish only the final artifact to the shared thread. Client work: implement a consistent Teams agent interaction contract.','An email identity supplied by a chat adapter is an input signal, not authorization proof; bind approval to your identity system.','Prototype one Teams intake flow: acknowledge → private approval → public completion.'),
('Ephemeral Messages — Chat SDK','https://chat-sdk.dev/docs/ephemeral-messages','docs','unknown','The SDK documents platform-specific persistence and required fallback behavior for private messages.','The same API has materially different records behavior across Teams, Slack, Google Chat, and Discord.','Buildn: define which approvals must become durable tickets. Client work: choose DM fallback deliberately, not as an accidental audit trail.','Slack ephemeral messages disappear on reload; Discord generally falls back to a persistent DM outside interaction responses.','Write a retention decision beside each agent approval action.'),
('Limit remote control to managed devices','https://github.blog/changelog/2026-07-30-limit-remote-control-to-managed-devices','release','2026-07-30','GitHub added device-level remote-control eligibility through a managed `remoteControl` setting, including requireSSO, disabled, and enabled modes.','Remote control changes the risk profile of an agent session; device posture is a useful enforcement layer beyond an account policy.','Buildn: keep remote control disabled on shared runners. Client work: deploy requireSSO through MDM for approved operator workstations.','This complements, rather than replaces, the enterprise-level remote-control policy.','Classify devices that may host remote control, then deploy the restrictive default.') ]},
{'slug':'attributed-workflow-operations','title':'Attributed Workflow Operations','rationale':'A practical operations lane separated from the recently covered agent-economics theme: fresh Vercel releases make both individual workflow investigations and tag-level AI cost attribution more usable in the same operating loop.','readout':'Instrument work before optimizing it. Searchable workflow runs identify the failing slice; request tags turn model spend into client-, feature-, and environment-level evidence.','items':[
('Expanded search for workflow runs in Vercel Observability','https://vercel.com/changelog/expanded-search-for-workflow-runs-in-vercel-observability','release','unknown','Vercel Workflows now supports structured run filters for workflow, environment, deployment ID, region, and custom attributes, with shareable URL queries.','An incident can now be narrowed to a reproducible slice instead of a vague time window.','Buildn: place a stable run attribute on every client workflow. Client work: add a saved incident query to each runbook.','Search does not create correlation data; schema and attributes must be designed at dispatch time.','Add client, environment, workflow, and release identifiers to one production workflow.'),
('Custom reporting on AI Gateway','https://vercel.com/changelog/custom-reporting-ai-gateway','release','unknown','AI Gateway beta reporting groups cost and usage by model, provider, user, and request tags, including BYOK traffic.','It can make agent margins and client allocations inspectable without maintaining a separate provider-console spreadsheet.','Buildn: tag every request with client, workflow, environment, and service tier. Client work: export a weekly feature-cost view.','It is beta, Pro/Enterprise-only, and uses paid cardinality and query pricing; do not put unbounded IDs into tags.','Define a four-field tag taxonomy and test one reporting query.'),
('Vercel Observability documentation','https://vercel.com/docs/observability','docs','unknown','The docs map request, function, external API, and AI Gateway signals across team and project scopes.','It supplies the broader causal trail around a workflow run: route, function, external dependency, then model request.','Buildn: link workflow run IDs from delivery artifacts. Client work: use project-level views for service debugging and team-level views for portfolio patterns.','Retention and granularity vary by plan and selected projects.','Document the minimum trace path from user request to model cost.') ]}
]
ledger={'date':DATE,'generated_at':datetime.datetime.now(datetime.timezone.utc).isoformat(),'editorial_thesis':'The strongest fresh signal is operational control at the seams: manage model replacement, keep agent interactions private and bounded, and make workflow execution and AI spend attributable.','topic_groups':[]}
for lane in lanes:
 ledger['topic_groups'].append({'slug':lane['slug'],'title':lane['title'],'selection_rationale':lane['rationale'],'sources':[{'title':x[0],'url':x[1],'source_type':x[2],'published_or_updated':x[3],'why_selected':x[5],'usefulness':x[6]} for x in lane['items']]})
(OUT/f'daily-ingest-{STAMP}.json').write_text(json.dumps(ledger,indent=2)+'\n')

def logo(): return '<svg viewBox="0 0 42 42" width="23" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 38 8 5h27l-3 24-7 6H4Z" fill="#01dc82"/><path d="M16 10l-1 9h10l-1 9h-10" fill="none" stroke="#033330" stroke-width="4"/></svg>'
def diagram(lane):
 names=['INTAKE','CONTROL','EVIDENCE']; fills=['#e8fff4','#fff8db','#eef2ff']
 if lane['slug']=='model-portfolio-change-control': names=['CATALOG','TEAM POLICY','TESTED FALLBACK']
 if lane['slug']=='private-agent-channel-controls': names=['SHARED INTAKE','PRIVATE APPROVAL','MANAGED TAKEOVER']
 if lane['slug']=='attributed-workflow-operations': names=['RUN ATTRIBUTES','FILTERED TRACE','COST REPORT']
 boxes=''.join(f'<rect x="{12+i*172}" y="55" width="142" height="64" rx="8" fill="{fills[i]}" stroke="#cbd5e1"/><text x="{83+i*172}" y="91" text-anchor="middle" class="label">{names[i]}</text>' for i in range(3))
 arrows=''.join(f'<path d="M{154+i*172} 87 H{181+i*172}" stroke="#01a967" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#a)"/>' for i in range(2))
 return f'<div class="diagram"><svg viewBox="0 0 520 170" role="img" aria-label="{html.escape(lane["title"])} signal map"><defs><marker id="a" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="8" refX="6" refY="3" orient="auto"><path d="M0,0 L6,3 L0,6z" fill="#01a967"/></marker></defs><text x="12" y="24" class="cap">OPERATING LOOP</text>{boxes}{arrows}<text x="260" y="149" text-anchor="middle" class="small">design the boundary before the automation</text></svg></div>'
def render(lane):
 cards=''.join(f'''<article class="item"><div class="badges"><span class="badge good">{html.escape(x[2])}</span><span class="badge">{html.escape(x[3])}</span></div><h3><a href="{html.escape(x[1])}">{html.escape(x[0])}</a></h3><dl><dt>What changed</dt><dd>{html.escape(x[4])}</dd><dt>Why it matters</dt><dd>{html.escape(x[5])}</dd><dt>Buildn / client use</dt><dd>{html.escape(x[6])}</dd><dt>Caveat</dt><dd>{html.escape(x[7])}</dd><dt>Follow-up</dt><dd><strong>{html.escape(x[8])}</strong></dd></dl></article>''' for x in lane['items'])
 rows=''.join('<tr><th>'+html.escape(x[0])+'</th><td>✓</td><td>✓</td><td>✓</td><td>✓</td></tr>' for x in lane['items'])
 links=''.join(f'<li><a href="{html.escape(x[1])}">{html.escape(x[0])}</a> <span>— {html.escape(x[2])}</span></li>' for x in lane['items'])
 return f'''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Daily Ingest Dossier — {html.escape(lane['title'])} — {DATE}</title><link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com"><link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin><link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Newsreader:opsz,wght@6..72,400;6..72,600&family=Plus+Jakarta+Sans:wght@400;500;600;700&display=swap" rel="stylesheet"><style>:root{{--brand:#01dc82;--deep:#033330;--lime:#cfe66a;--red:#b3261e;--amber:#9a6700;--ink:#0f172a;--muted:#475569;--line:#e2e8f0;--bg:#fafaf9;--card:#fff;--serif:"Newsreader",Georgia,serif;--sans:"Plus Jakarta Sans",system-ui,sans-serif}}*{{box-sizing:border-box}}body{{margin:0;background:var(--bg);color:var(--ink);font:15px/1.6 var(--sans)}}main{{max-width:900px;margin:auto;padding:42px 20px 70px}}.wordmark{{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;font-weight:700;color:var(--deep)}}header{{margin-bottom:28px}}h1,h2,h3{{font-family:var(--serif);color:var(--deep)}}h1{{font-size:2.35rem;line-height:1.12;margin:12px 0 8px}}h2{{font-size:1.45rem;margin:0 0 8px}}h3{{font-size:1.18rem;margin:7px 0}}p{{margin:.5rem 0}}.date,.cap,.small{{font:11px ui-monospace,monospace;color:var(--muted);letter-spacing:.06em}}.card{{background:var(--card);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:13px;padding:22px;margin:17px 0}}.diagram{{border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:10px;padding:11px;margin:14px 0;background:#fff}}svg{{display:block;width:100%;height:auto}}.label{{font:600 10px var(--sans);fill:#334155;letter-spacing:.04em}}.small{{fill:#64748b}}.badges{{display:flex;gap:6px;flex-wrap:wrap}}.badge{{font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;font-weight:700;padding:3px 7px;border-radius:5px;background:#eef2f7;color:#475569}}.good{{background:#dcfce7;color:#166534}}.item{{border-top:1px solid var(--line);padding:19px 0}}.item:first-of-type{{border-top:0;padding-top:0}}a{{color:#087c54}}dl{{margin:10px 0 0;display:grid;grid-template-columns:145px 1fr;gap:6px 14px}}dt{{font-weight:700;color:var(--deep)}}dd{{margin:0}}table{{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:13px}}th,td{{padding:9px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);text-align:left}}td{{text-align:center;color:#087c54;font-weight:700}}.actions{{padding-left:20px}}.actions li{{margin:7px 0}}.callout{{border-left:3px solid var(--amber);background:#fffbeb;padding:10px 13px;color:#713f12}}.trail{{padding-left:19px}}.trail span{{color:var(--muted)}}@media(max-width:580px){{dl{{grid-template-columns:1fr}}dt{{margin-top:7px}}}}</style></head><body><main><header><div class="wordmark">{logo()}<span>Buildn</span></div><div class="date">DAILY INGEST DOSSIER · {DATE}</div><h1>{html.escape(lane['title'])}</h1><p>{html.escape(lane['readout'])}</p></header><section class="card"><h2>Signal map</h2>{diagram(lane)}<p class="callout">Selection rationale — {html.escape(lane['rationale'])}</p></section><section class="card"><h2>Dossier cards</h2>{cards}</section><section class="card"><h2>Use-case matrix</h2><table><thead><tr><th>Signal</th><th>Buildn OS</th><th>Client work</th><th>Agent workflows</th><th>Personal leverage</th></tr></thead><tbody>{rows}</tbody></table></section><section class="card"><h2>Top actions</h2><ol class="actions">{''.join('<li>'+html.escape(x[8])+'</li>' for x in lane['items'])}</ol></section><section class="card"><h2>Source trail</h2><ul class="trail">{links}</ul></section></main></body></html>'''
for lane in lanes: (OUT/f'daily-ingest-{lane["slug"]}-{STAMP}.html').write_text(render(lane))
# Overview
cards=''.join(f'<article class="card"><div class="tag">SELECTED LANE</div><h2>{html.escape(x["title"])}</h2><p>{html.escape(x["rationale"])}</p><a href="daily-ingest-{x["slug"]}-{STAMP}.html">Open dossier →</a></article>' for x in lanes)
top='<ol>'+''.join(f'<li><strong>{html.escape(x["items"][0][0])}</strong> — {html.escape(x["items"][0][8])}</li>' for x in lanes)+'</ol>'
over=f'''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Daily Ingest Dossier — Overview — {DATE}</title><link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com"><link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin><link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Newsreader:opsz,wght@6..72,400;6..72,600&family=Plus+Jakarta+Sans:wght@400;500;600;700&display=swap" rel="stylesheet"><style>:root{{--brand:#01dc82;--deep:#033330;--line:#e2e8f0;--bg:#fafaf9;--card:#fff;--muted:#475569;--serif:"Newsreader",Georgia,serif;--sans:"Plus Jakarta Sans",system-ui,sans-serif}}*{{box-sizing:border-box}}body{{margin:0;background:var(--bg);color:#0f172a;font:16px/1.6 var(--sans)}}main{{max-width:900px;margin:auto;padding:42px 20px 70px}}.wordmark{{display:flex;gap:8px;align-items:center;color:var(--deep);font-weight:700}}h1,h2{{font-family:var(--serif);color:var(--deep)}}h1{{font-size:2.5rem;line-height:1.1;margin:14px 0 8px}}h2{{margin:0 0 6px}}.date,.tag{{font:11px ui-monospace,monospace;letter-spacing:.08em;color:var(--muted)}}.grid{{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(230px,1fr));gap:14px}}.card{{background:var(--card);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:13px;padding:21px}}a{{color:#087c54;font-weight:700}}.top{{margin-top:17px;border-left:3px solid var(--brand)}}li{{margin:8px 0}}</style></head><body><main><header><div class="wordmark">{logo()}<span>Buildn</span></div><div class="date">DAILY INGEST DOSSIER · {DATE}</div><h1>Control the seams</h1><p>Today’s practical advantage is operational control at the seams: manage model replacement, keep agent interactions private and bounded, and make workflow execution and AI spend attributable.</p></header><section class="grid">{cards}</section><section class="card top"><h2>All-lanes top three</h2>{top}</section></main></body></html>'''
(OUT/f'daily-ingest-overview-{STAMP}.html').write_text(over)
